# ===========================================
# Frontend Configuration (apps/frontend)
# ===========================================
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is embedded in the
# browser bundle, so none of them may hold a secret.

# ===========================================
# Backend API
# ===========================================
# Base URL of the FastAPI backend as seen from the *browser*. Leave as '/' to
# use the Next.js proxy (next.config.ts rewrites /api/* to BACKEND_ORIGIN),
# which is what you want for local development and single-host deployments.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=/

# Where the Next.js server proxies /api/* to. Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000.
# BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# Client + proxy request timeout in ms. MUST equal the backend's
# REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS x 1000 — the shortest of the three layers aborts
# first, so raising only one has no effect. Bounded to [30_000, 1_800_000].
# NEXT_PUBLIC_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=240000

# ===========================================
# Authentication (Supabase, Google OAuth only)
# ===========================================
# Google is the only sign-in method; there is no email/password flow. Supabase
# owns identity, and the frontend forwards its access token to the backend,
# which verifies it and partitions all data by the user id inside it.
#
# Leave BOTH values blank for single-user local mode: no sign-in screen, and
# all data belongs to one implicit local account. Setting them is what switches
# the app into multi-user mode, and the backend's SUPABASE_URL must be set to
# the same project (see apps/backend/.env.example) or the two will disagree.
#
# Setup, once, in your Supabase project:
#   1. Authentication -> Sign In / Providers -> enable Google, and paste the
#      client ID + secret from a Google Cloud OAuth 2.0 Web application.
#   2. In Google Cloud, add this Authorized redirect URI:
#        https://<your-project>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#   3. In Supabase, Authentication -> URL Configuration:
#        Site URL:      http://localhost:3000        (your real origin in prod)
#        Redirect URLs: http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
#                       https://your-domain/auth/callback
#
# Both values below are publishable by design — the anon key only permits what
# your Supabase policies permit.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key
